    "q-42811": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42811",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication.",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
