    "q-32039": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32039",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication.",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
