    "q-75113": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75113",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the three given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-75113-a",
              "type": "math",
